{#-
  Palworld dedicated server settings -- MANAGED BY PYINFRA, DO NOT EDIT ON THE HOST.

  The engine wants every setting on one `OptionSettings=(...)` line, which makes an unreviewable
  8 KB diff out of any single change. So this template keeps one setting per line and joins them
  at render time. The full default set is carried explicitly rather than only the handful we
  override, so the whole world configuration is visible in git and a game update changing an
  upstream default cannot silently change this server's rules. Overridden: ServerName,
  ServerDescription, ServerPassword, AdminPassword, ServerPlayerMaxNum, PublicPort, RCONEnabled,
  RCONPort. Everything else is Pocketpair's shipped default, generated from
  DefaultPalWorldSettings.ini.

  DO NOT "TIDY UP" THE OUTPUT FORMAT. The server rewrites this file itself when it shuts down,
  normalising it: `;` comments are stripped and the file ends with a blank line. Our render has
  to match that normalised form byte-for-byte, or files.template sees a diff on every single
  deploy and restarts a live game server to "apply" a change that isn't one. That is why the
  documentation you are reading is a Jinja comment (renders to nothing) instead of `;` lines,
  and why there is a trailing blank line below. Verified by checksum against the engine's own
  rewrite -- if you change the layout, re-verify it.
-#}
